(6356666, 940432, 129583, '<td valign="top">Because of the way the sunlight through the jug is coloring the water, it makes it a bit of an unappealing browny/orange, there is a real physical turn-off of that becomes a visual turn-off for the photo (for me personally).  I do like how gigantic the jug looks though, it is quite monumental.</td>', 'Because of the way the sunlight through the jug is coloring the water, it makes it a bit of an unappealing browny/orange, there is a real physical turn-off of that becomes a visual turn-off for the photo (for me personally).  I do like how gigantic the jug looks though, it is quite monumental.', '2011-03-19 03:32:21.000000', NULL, 1),
(6356667, 940132, 129583, '<td valign="top">The flash has added some nice highlights in the sink, but also caused a nasty shadow from the faucet.  I also do not really understand the concept behind putting the bottle in the sink beyond the obvious.  Why did you decide to include the time stamp?</td>', 'The flash has added some nice highlights in the sink, but also caused a nasty shadow from the faucet.  I also do not really understand the concept behind putting the bottle in the sink beyond the obvious.  Why did you decide to include the time stamp?', '2011-03-19 03:37:42.000000', NULL, 1),
(6356680, 939901, 67258, '<td valign="top">Rather well done!</td>', 'Rather well done!', '2011-03-19 05:06:52.000000', NULL, 1),
(6356707, 940972, 69325, '<td valign="top">I think what hurt you in this shot was the subject itself. In my opinion, water bottle just is not interestig enough to make compelling shots out it. So to be successful the shot is really going to have to have a ''wow'' factor (tough in basic editing) so while you have a technically sound shot here that would do well for stock photography or even an ad for camelbak, it''s not enough to elicit comments or votes from the viewers. if i could change anything about the shot it may be the lighting. not sure what you''re working with for lighting so that may not be possible.</td>', 'I think what hurt you in this shot was the subject itself. In my opinion, water bottle just is not interestig enough to make compelling shots out it. So to be successful the shot is really going to have to have a ''wow'' factor (tough in basic editing) so while you have a technically sound shot here that would do well for stock photography or even an ad for camelbak, it''s not enough to elicit comments or votes from the viewers. if i could change anything about the shot it may be the lighting. not sure what you''re working with for lighting so that may not be possible.', '2011-03-19 07:38:31.000000', NULL, 1),
