(6357468, 940972, 117474, '<td valign="top">I like the diagonalisation of this. Negative space concentrates the eyes on the subjects. <br/>Colours are nice and rich. I gave this 6 ''cause it fitted the subject of the challenge, is nicely composed, nicely lighted and sharp. I didn''t score it higher cause I didn''t find the subject very engaging, to be honest. <br/>One thing that struck me was about the blue bottle. The few drops of water in the blue bottle are a little out of place, I think. I don''t see the counterpart drops in the red bottle, and I find this image so wonderfully symmetric that I feel disappointed it''s not there :) I think the image would have been better either if they weren''t there at all or if they were also on the red bottle. Not sure if it''d''ve made me score higher though. I''d have to see it otherwise.</td>', 'I like the diagonalisation of this. Negative space concentrates the eyes on the subjects. Colours are nice and rich. I gave this 6 ''cause it fitted the subject of the challenge, is nicely composed, nicely lighted and sharp. I didn''t score it higher cause I didn''t find the subject very engaging, to be honest. One thing that struck me was about the blue bottle. The few drops of water in the blue bottle are a little out of place, I think. I don''t see the counterpart drops in the red bottle, and I find this image so wonderfully symmetric that I feel disappointed it''s not there :) I think the image would have been better either if they weren''t there at all or if they were also on the red bottle. Not sure if it''d''ve made me score higher though. I''d have to see it otherwise.', '2011-03-20 09:47:55.000000', NULL, 1),
(6357570, 940875, 55283, '<td valign="top">Nice shot. I gave you a 7. You caught a nice, crisp drip. What I really liked was the water tension holding the overflow together in the bottle. You just know that the "last drop" won''t fit. It creates a moderate amount of dramatic tension, but it''s still just water. The theme, as you know, made it difficult to make a super interesting shot. I think you''ve done pretty well.<br/>My nitpicks:<br/>The front of the sink in the bottom left corner. It actually probably helps the image, as I don''t think it would be as good without some foreground, but it still bugs me. I can''t really put my finger on it.<br/>The faucet itself probably should have been wiped down to remove the spots before shooting. That''s my biggest peeve with the execution here.<br/>Finally, I''d like to see some more contrast. As a b/w image, you are only working with tonalities and I''d like the bottle to stick out just a little bit more. A bit more "pop." But, I usually overprocess my stuff, so take that with a grain of salt.</td>', 'Nice shot. I gave you a 7. You caught a nice, crisp drip. What I really liked was the water tension holding the overflow together in the bottle. You just know that the "last drop" won''t fit. It creates a moderate amount of dramatic tension, but it''s still just water. The theme, as you know, made it difficult to make a super interesting shot. I think you''ve done pretty well.My nitpicks:The front of the sink in the bottom left corner. It actually probably helps the image, as I don''t think it would be as good without some foreground, but it still bugs me. I can''t really put my finger on it.The faucet itself probably should have been wiped down to remove the spots before shooting. That''s my biggest peeve with the execution here.Finally, I''d like to see some more contrast. As a b/w image, you are only working with tonalities and I''d like the bottle to stick out just a little bit more. A bit more "pop." But, I usually overprocess my stuff, so take that with a grain of salt.', '2011-03-20 13:08:34.000000', NULL, 1),
