(6361032, 940811, 114969, '<td valign="top">Oliver, very high quality photo as usual. Congratulations on the ribbon!<br/> <br/>As for the DoF debate, the top of the bottle being out of focus did not bother me: in fact, I liked it, because it puts the emphasis even more on the splash''s sharpness.<br/> <br/>In order to obtain everything in focus, obviously, composing 2 exposures would work, as you explained. Just wondering: why didn''t you simply raised the ISO, especially with a 5D2? This would have allowed for a narrower aperture, wouldn''t it?</td>', 'Oliver, very high quality photo as usual. Congratulations on the ribbon! As for the DoF debate, the top of the bottle being out of focus did not bother me: in fact, I liked it, because it puts the emphasis even more on the splash''s sharpness. In order to obtain everything in focus, obviously, composing 2 exposures would work, as you explained. Just wondering: why didn''t you simply raised the ISO, especially with a 5D2? This would have allowed for a narrower aperture, wouldn''t it?', '2011-03-23 09:08:15.000000', NULL, 0),
(6361045, 940810, 91360, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by vawendy:</b></div><hr/><i> wheee!!!! Irene is back!!!<br/> <br/>Ummmm... wait... Irene''s too good. That means less ribbons for everyone else...<br/> <br/>Drat!!!!! Irene is back!!!<br/> <br/>Wait... but I didn''t enter water bottle...<br/> <br/>Wheee!!!! Irene is back!!! </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>LOL!!!!!!!!<br/>there is nothing in the world that can cure you better then self acomplishment and the joy of creation.<br/> <br/>by the way..I rad an article that found after a long statistics research that photographers live longer then other occupations..:)</td>', 'Originally posted by vawendy: wheee!!!! Irene is back!!! Ummmm... wait... Irene''s too good. That means less ribbons for everyone else... Drat!!!!! Irene is back!!! Wait... but I didn''t enter water bottle... Wheee!!!! Irene is back!!!   LOL!!!!!!!!there is nothing in the world that can cure you better then self acomplishment and the joy of creation. by the way..I rad an article that found after a long statistics research that photographers live longer then other occupations..:)', '2011-03-23 09:25:47.000000', NULL, 0),
(6361053, 940811, 49109, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by gyaban:</b></div><hr/><i> Just wondering: why didn''t you simply raised the ISO, especially with a 5D2? This would have allowed for a narrower aperture, wouldn''t it? </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Absolutely true, but I wanted the back edge of the table to be blurred as much as possible. And when I looked at the shot on the camera display it seemed to be enough DOF for the bottle. Reshooting was no ootion timewise.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2011-03-23 16:31:16.</i></td>', 'Originally posted by gyaban: Just wondering: why didn''t you simply raised the ISO, especially with a 5D2? This would have allowed for a narrower aperture, wouldn''t it?   Absolutely true, but I wanted the back edge of the table to be blurred as much as possible. And when I looked at the shot on the camera display it seemed to be enough DOF for the bottle. Reshooting was no ootion timewise.', '2011-03-23 09:32:04.000000', '2011-03-23 16:31:16.000000', 0),
(6361113, 940810, 3936, '<td valign="top">How great it is to have you back!<br/> <br/>And what a way to come back, with a blue ribbon!<br/> <br/>Congratulations, and I''m very glad to hear that you are feeling better.  <br/> <br/>As Lydiatoo would say, Life is indeed good...</td>', 'How great it is to have you back! And what a way to come back, with a blue ribbon! Congratulations, and I''m very glad to hear that you are feeling better.   As Lydiatoo would say, Life is indeed good...', '2011-03-23 10:17:03.000000', NULL, 0),
